WEBVTT

00:00:00.504 --> 00:00:06.378
Hi, I'm an AI scientist. This simulation shows how we design enzymes

00:00:06.378 --> 00:00:07.846
to target biofilm.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:13.191
Biofilm is a layer of bacteria held together by a sticky mesh.

00:00:13.191 --> 00:00:16.972
Some of that mesh is DNA outside the cells.

00:00:17.274 --> 00:00:22.966
Watch the enzyme fold. It is a chain of amino acids, and

00:00:22.966 --> 00:00:28.658
its shape creates an active site: tiny molecular scissors. Our starting enzyme,

00:00:28.658 --> 00:00:30.080
NucB, cuts DNA.

00:00:30.384 --> 00:00:37.037
Boltz predicted its shape. Through Tamarind Bio, MutRank explored changes and Hyper

00:00:37.037 --> 00:00:43.690
M P N N generated new sequences while we kept known cutting

00:00:43.690 --> 00:00:44.799
positions unchanged.

00:00:45.102 --> 00:00:49.590
Finally, the heat animation illustrates how an enzyme can lose its shape.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:54.077
Our goal is to redesign the surrounding chain so the scissors keep

00:00:54.077 --> 00:00:56.320
their shape in a cooling loop.
